  "live_records": {
    "q-171839": {
      "dom_id": "step-q171839",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the truth set of $P(x)⇔Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the universal set $R:$\n\n- $P(x):$ $2x+1\\le 7$\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x>1$",
      "worked_solution": "Since we have that\n\n$$\nP(x)⇔Q(x)≡(P(x)∧Q(x))∨(¬P(x)∧¬Q(x)),\n$$\n\n \n\nthe corresponding truth set can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P⇔Q}=({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we note the following:\n\n- To find the the truth set of $P(x),$ we solve the inequality:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+1 & \\le 7 \\\\ 2x & \\le 6 \\\\ x & \\le 3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the truth set of $P(x)$ is\n${T}_{P}=(-\\infty ,3]$\nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}=(3,\\infty ).$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n${T}_{Q}=(1,\\infty )$ \nand its complement is\n${\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}=(-\\infty ,1].$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} & =(-\\infty ,3]\\cap (1,\\infty ) \\\\  & =(1,3] \\\\ {\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q} & =(3,\\infty )\\cap (-\\infty ,1] \\\\  & =∅ \\\\ {T}_{P⇔Q} & =({T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q})\\cup ({\\overset{―}{T}}_{P}\\cap {\\overset{―}{T}}_{Q}) \\\\  & =(1,3]\\cup ∅ \\\\  & =(1,3].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
