    "q-183358": {
      "dom_id": "step-q183358",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the following predicates.\n\n$\\,$ $A(x):$ $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$ $\\,$ $B(x):$ $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$ \n\nWhich of the following is equivalent to the biconditional predicate $A(x)⇔B(x)?$\n\nI. $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ if and only if $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\nII. If $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ then $x\\in {Z}^{-},$ or if $x\\in {Z}^{-}$ then $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$\n\nIII. $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$",
      "worked_solution": "A biconditional expression $P⇔Q≡(P⇒Q)∧(Q⇒P)$ can be read as shown below:\n\n- $P$ if and only if $Q$\n\n- $P$ is equivalent to $Q$\n\n- If $P$ then $Q,$ and if $Q$ then $P$\n\nSo, $A⇔B$ translates into the following sentences:\n\n- $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ if and only if $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\n- $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ is equivalent to  $x\\in {Z}^{-}.$\n\n- If $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}$ then $x\\in {Z}^{-},$ and if $x\\in {Z}^{-}$ then $x\\in Z∖{N}_{0}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
